Negative control for LookupRenderer.test.ts (B6/AC8 no-service fallback).

Removes the `hasOption("lookup")` clause from the renderer's tester, so LookupRenderer
greedily claims a plain Control that carries no lookup bag instead of letting it fall
back to the plain input renderer. The AC8 assertion that a service-less control renders
a `data-test-key="input"` (not a combobox) goes red.

diff --git a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/LookupRenderer.vue b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/LookupRenderer.vue
index 44f2e458d..66a1b3faa 100644
--- a/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/LookupRenderer.vue
+++ b/packages/client-vue/src/components/form/renderers/LookupRenderer.vue
@@ -126,6 +126,6 @@ onBeforeUnmount(() => debouncedSearch.cancel());
 <script lang="ts">
 export const tester = {
   rank: 3,
-  controlType: and(uiTypeIs("Control"), hasOption("lookup"))
+  controlType: uiTypeIs("Control")
 };
 </script>
